; WildGrass — the Wild grass terrain tile (emits *nothing*, the inert-land invariant's
; structural source — see terrain.md, spec.md Open Question #29). Reuses the same
; Grass_Common_Short.gltf mesh as true Grass (CC0, Quaternius, Stylized Nature MegaKit —
; see project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres); no new source
; for this rework either.
;
; MULTIMESH REWORK (2026-08-16, human-reported): same complaint that drove
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's rework — "grass and wild grass... still spotty... shorter
; height, and more instances (30+)" — applied here too, same technique (a single
; MultiMeshInstance3D, "WildGrassMultiMesh" below, instead of 30+ individual scene-tree
; nodes; see GrassCommonShort.tscn's header for the full "why not just add more
; MeshInstance3D nodes" reasoning, identical here).
;
; STILL DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT FROM TRUE GRASS, not a copy of it — this is a PROPOSED
; treatment for Open Question #29 ("must read as something to claim, without reading as
; broken"), not its closure:
;   - 32 instances (vs. Grass's 36) — still clears "30+", but a lower count than true
;     Grass, continuing the prior version's "thinner growth" intent.
;   - CLUSTERED, not evenly scattered: 4 cluster centers with UNEVEN per-cluster counts
;     (10, 6, 10, 6 — not a uniform 8/8/8/8) so coverage reads patchy/untended rather than
;     as a uniform lawn, with real gaps of bare ground between clusters. Grass, by
;     contrast, scatters evenly across the whole tile. Deterministic, fixed-seed build
;     (seed 20260817, distinct from Grass's 20260816) — one baked pattern, not randomized
;     per tile at runtime.
;   - 3 small bare-dirt PlaneMesh patches (up from 2 previously) placed in the gaps between
;     clusters, reinforcing the "bald spots" cue.
;   - Slab tint stays the duller, drier olive-khaki (Color(0.55, 0.52, 0.3, 1)) vs. true
;     Grass's saturated green (Color(0.42, 0.68, 0.3, 1)) — unchanged from the prior pass.
;
; HEIGHT REDUCED: scale baseline dropped to 0.065 (+/-22% jitter) — shorter than
; GrassCommonShort's new 0.075 baseline, continuing this terrain's existing "smaller than
; true Grass" convention from the original hand-placed version. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF,
; same as GrassCommonShort's baseline — no GDD number exists for grass height, and whether
; this reads as "something to claim" per #29's exact wording is the human's eyeball call,
; not tech-art's to settle.
;
; MESH EMBEDDED, NOT ExtResource-REFERENCED, and BUILT VIA A ONE-OFF HEADLESS SCRIPT: same
; reasoning and the same MultiMesh-buffer / dummy-RenderingServer caveat as
; GrassCommonShort.tscn's header — see there for the full explanation, identical here.
;
; EVERYTHING NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (unchanged requirement from the prior
; pass): wild grass is the world's default untouched-land terrain, so it is the "old"
; visual sitting under nearly every tile a player ever repaints to Forest — see this
; scene's original header (preserved in content-pipeline-status.md's `wild_grass` row) and
; CommonTree1.tscn's header for the full OcclusionFader-exemption mechanism this protects
; against. The ground box, all 3 bare-dirt patches, and the multimesh are all children of
; one wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab".
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap — a separate
; complaint from the density one above, fixed in the same pass): same fix, same exact-1.0-
; match reasoning as GrassCommonShort.tscn's header. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
